Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:09:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: keep the staggered fast scroller thumb steady

The thumb position was estimated from the average height of the items
currently on screen. A panorama grid mixes 3:2 and 2:3 cells, so that
average changed whenever the window did and the thumb jumped.

Heights are now recorded per index as items are measured. The average
moves only when a stored height changes, and items not seen yet use
that average. Full-line rows (search bar, section header) are left out
of the average; LazyStaggeredGridItemInfo does not expose the span, so
a row is recognised by being wider than a lane cell. Lane count is the
most columns observed so far. Dragging still maps the thumb to
scrollToItem(laneCount * row, offset within the row).

Item offset does not include beforeContentPadding (padding is applied
at placement), so the scroll offset follows the content position and
the padding is added only to the scroll range.

Harmony-only: the estimate is line-identical in mihon-harmony 0016 and
anikku-harmony 0023; Animeko does not use this scroller.
